WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.876
Previously on Love Live!

00:00:01.876 --> 00:00:03.837
The Halloween event was a success.

00:00:03.837 --> 00:00:06.047
As we began working toward Love Live,

00:00:06.047 --> 00:00:07.591
we discovered something wrong
with Honoka-chan's body.

00:00:09.634 --> 00:00:11.052
And mine.

00:00:11.386 --> 00:00:14.556
Having gained weight,
Honoka-chan and I began dieting.

00:00:14.931 --> 00:00:17.976
Meanwhile, a mistake with the student
council caused even more problems.

00:00:17.976 --> 00:00:20.854
Shouldn't we handle this ourselves?

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:23.189
Through the efforts of
Honoka-chan and her friends,

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:25.525
the student council escaped its predicament.

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:29.487
Even our diets were successful. And
the final preliminaries are coming up!

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:34.951
We now present the final group
moving on to the final preliminaries.

00:00:34.951 --> 00:00:38.788
Otonokizaka High's school idol group, p's!

00:00:40.749 --> 00:00:45.337
One of these four groups will
be advancing to Love Live.

00:00:45.337 --> 00:00:48.089
Let's hear what each group hopes to achieve!

00:00:48.089 --> 00:00:49.758
Starting with p's!

00:00:49.758 --> 00:00:51.092
Oh, okay!

00:00:51.092 --> 00:00:57.057
W-We've always been working
toward winning Love Live.

00:00:57.057 --> 00:01:00.727
So, we'll definitely win!

00:01:03.813 --> 00:01:04.731
Huh?

00:01:04.731 --> 00:01:08.193
A-A-A-Amazing! What a
sudden declaration of victory!

00:01:08.193 --> 00:01:09.069
What?

00:01:09.861 --> 00:01:11.029
Idiot...

00:01:11.029 --> 00:01:12.697
She said it.

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:16.409
Finally...

00:01:17.535 --> 00:01:20.038
We're finally here...

00:01:20.038 --> 00:01:26.252
saa yume wo kanaeru no wa minna no yuuki Come
on... Our courage makes our dreams come true

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:33.843
makenai (kokoro de) ashita e kaketeyukou Let's
run toward tomorrow with unbeaten (hearts)

00:01:40.892 --> 00:01:46.231
Tsuyoi tsuyoi negaigoto ga
A strong, strong wish

00:01:46.231 --> 00:01:51.778
bokutachi wo michibiite kureta
Led us along

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:56.866
tsugi wa zettai yuzurenaiyo
We can't give up the next one

00:01:56.866 --> 00:02:02.038
nokosareta jikan wo nigirishimete We'll hold
on tightly to the time we have remaining

00:02:02.038 --> 00:02:07.502
tada no omoide sore dake ja iyadayo
We don't want only a memory

00:02:07.502 --> 00:02:13.341
seiippai chikara no kagiri hashirunda
We'll run as hard as we can

00:02:13.341 --> 00:02:16.219
(CHANCE FOR ME CHANCE FOR YOU)
(Chance for me! Chance for you!)

00:02:16.219 --> 00:02:21.808
Saa yume wo dakishimetara ue wo muite
Come on... Embrace your dreams and look up

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:26.646
kimi no sekai ga ohkiku kawaruyo
Your world will change dramatically

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:32.736
saa yume wo kanaeru no wa minna no yuuki Come
on... Our courage makes our dreams come true

00:02:32.736 --> 00:02:37.782
makenai (kokoro de) ashita e kaketeyukou Let's
run toward tomorrow with unbeaten (hearts)

00:02:37.782 --> 00:02:43.121
Ima koko de deaeta kiseki
The miracle that we met here and now

00:02:43.121 --> 00:02:49.836
wasurenaide bokutachi no kisetsu
Don't forget our season

00:02:51.588 --> 00:02:54.090
Why'd you have to openly declare we'd win!?

00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:56.259
I was just so excited...

00:02:56.259 --> 00:02:59.971
But we actually are trying to win,
so there shouldn't be a problem.

00:02:59.971 --> 00:03:02.390
You're right. Besides, A-RISE said...

00:03:02.974 --> 00:03:08.104
We believe this final preliminary
is on par with the main event.

00:03:09.063 --> 00:03:12.442
Oh, right. They've acknowledged our talent.

00:03:12.442 --> 00:03:16.029
Let's decide what song we're going
to sing at the final preliminary.

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:20.784
#8 - My Wish We can only sing one
song, so we should choose carefully.

00:03:20.784 --> 00:03:21.785
In order to win...

00:03:21.785 --> 00:03:24.204
I think we should sing a new song.

00:03:24.662 --> 00:03:25.789
A new song!

00:03:25.789 --> 00:03:27.290
Sounds interesting!

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:29.876
Since we had to sing a new song
at the regional preliminary,

00:03:29.876 --> 00:03:31.753
that may be the right choice.

00:03:31.753 --> 00:03:35.715
But, I don't know that we should
make our decision based on that...

00:03:35.715 --> 00:03:39.093
We don't know that a new song would
actually provide any advantage.

00:03:39.469 --> 00:03:44.307
Besides, like we said the other day, we
shouldn't force ourselves to do new things...

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:50.688
This is just a thought,
but what if we tried a love song?

00:03:52.816 --> 00:03:54.275
A love song!?

00:03:54.275 --> 00:03:54.943
I seel

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:58.613
Love songs are essential to idols!

00:03:58.613 --> 00:04:01.533
It's a standard part of everyone's set.

00:04:01.533 --> 00:04:04.118
But up till now, p's has never had one!

00:04:04.911 --> 00:04:05.787
Nozomi?

00:04:07.455 --> 00:04:11.668
But, why haven't we written a love song yet?

00:04:11.668 --> 00:04:12.585
Because...

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:16.339
Wh-Why are you all looking at me like that?

00:04:16.339 --> 00:04:19.717
You have no experience with romance, right?

00:04:19.717 --> 00:04:20.343
What?

00:04:20.802 --> 00:04:22.095
Why would you assume that?

00:04:22.846 --> 00:04:23.847
Then you do?

00:04:23.847 --> 00:04:24.639
Do you?

00:04:24.639 --> 00:04:27.600
Why are you so interested?

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:29.060
- Do you?
- Do you?

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:29.561
Do you?

00:04:29.561 --> 00:04:31.187
You, too!?

00:04:31.187 --> 00:04:32.647
- Well?
- Do you?

00:04:32.647 --> 00:04:33.106
Do you?

00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:35.900
Umi-chan, tell us! Which is it?

00:04:36.359 --> 00:04:37.569
Umi-chan...

00:04:37.902 --> 00:04:39.696
W-Well...

00:04:45.743 --> 00:04:47.078
I don't.

00:04:47.078 --> 00:04:49.163
I knew it.

00:04:49.163 --> 00:04:50.456
I was so surprised.

00:04:50.456 --> 00:04:53.459
You should've just said so!

00:04:53.459 --> 00:04:55.962
My heart was pounding!

00:04:55.962 --> 00:04:58.548
Why are you getting on my case about this?

00:04:58.548 --> 00:05:01.217
Honoka and Kotori, you don't
have any experience, either!

00:05:01.217 --> 00:05:01.926
Yeah.

00:05:01.926 --> 00:05:05.013
I'm not sure we can start
working on a new song now.

00:05:06.264 --> 00:05:09.350
But isn't it too soon to give up?

00:05:09.976 --> 00:05:10.768
Eli?

00:05:10.768 --> 00:05:15.940
You're right. The most important
part of song writing is imagination.

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:21.404
It's not as though I've only drawn
from my experiences in the past.

00:05:21.404 --> 00:05:25.241
But a love song is about romance, right?

00:05:25.241 --> 00:05:27.410
How are we supposed to get inspired?

00:05:28.328 --> 00:05:29.871
Well...

00:05:29.871 --> 00:05:30.705
For example...

00:05:34.918 --> 00:05:36.377
Please accept this!

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:38.212
Nice!

00:05:38.713 --> 00:05:41.090
Is this supposed to inspire us?

00:05:41.090 --> 00:05:41.799
Yes.

00:05:42.216 --> 00:05:46.095
The words you come up with in
these moments are fairly important.

00:05:46.095 --> 00:05:48.389
But why do we need a camera?

00:05:48.765 --> 00:05:51.184
It'll make her more anxious.

00:05:51.184 --> 00:05:55.146
Besides, we can enjoy these memories later.

00:05:55.146 --> 00:05:57.357
You're clearly after the latter.

00:05:57.357 --> 00:05:58.441
Now, now.

00:05:58.441 --> 00:06:00.693
Maki-chan, you're next.

00:06:00.693 --> 00:06:02.487
Wh-Why me?

00:06:04.197 --> 00:06:07.533
Here. Just take it.

00:06:08.201 --> 00:06:11.579
I-It's not like you're the only
person I gave one to...

00:06:11.579 --> 00:06:13.164
Don't get the wrong idea!

00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:16.751
Perfect! That was perfect!

00:06:16.751 --> 00:06:18.086
I've seen that in a manga!

00:06:18.461 --> 00:06:20.630
Well? Are you satisfied now?

00:06:21.297 --> 00:06:22.632
Don't get ahead of yourself.

00:06:23.007 --> 00:06:24.926
I'm not.

00:06:24.926 --> 00:06:26.844
Nico-cchi, would you like to try?

00:06:27.971 --> 00:06:31.307
Sheesh. You're all so hopeless.

00:06:34.519 --> 00:06:37.855
What's wrong? You mean you don't know?

00:06:38.314 --> 00:06:40.525
No! Don't look. It's embarrassing.

00:06:42.527 --> 00:06:46.614
My, you're hopeless, aren't you?
All right, just a little.

00:06:47.991 --> 00:06:52.495
You said you liked my hair down, didn't you?

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:59.210
I'll give it to you...
A special and happy Love-Nic—

00:07:00.628 --> 00:07:01.713
I'm out of batteries.

00:07:01.713 --> 00:07:03.089
Why!?

00:07:05.258 --> 00:07:08.094
We didn't settle on anything.

00:07:08.094 --> 00:07:09.637
It's not easy.

00:07:09.637 --> 00:07:12.432
Maybe we shouldn't force ourselves.

00:07:12.432 --> 00:07:14.017
This is for the final preliminary.

00:07:14.392 --> 00:07:18.271
You're right. The final preliminaries are the
culmination of what we've done so far.

00:07:18.604 --> 00:07:23.651
I feel like doing our best at the things
we've done so far is most important.

00:07:23.651 --> 00:07:26.029
I agree.

00:07:26.029 --> 00:07:26.738
Yeah.

00:07:26.738 --> 00:07:30.366
But I'd like to work on it a little more.

00:07:30.366 --> 00:07:31.617
What?

00:07:31.617 --> 00:07:32.994
Eli?

00:07:32.994 --> 00:07:35.371
Eli-chan, are you opposed to it?

00:07:35.371 --> 00:07:40.626
I'm not opposed, but I think a
love song would be strong.

00:07:40.626 --> 00:07:42.754
I feel like we can't win without one.

00:07:43.379 --> 00:07:44.881
You think so?

00:07:44.881 --> 00:07:46.632
But it's not easy...

00:07:46.632 --> 00:07:50.011
Besides, Nozomi's usually right.

00:07:51.596 --> 00:07:54.766
Why don't we think it over a little more, then?

00:07:54.766 --> 00:07:57.518
I don't mind either way.

00:07:57.518 --> 00:08:02.273
Why don't we get together and
exchange ideas this Sunday?

00:08:03.107 --> 00:08:06.736
I'll look for something that might help us.

00:08:06.736 --> 00:08:08.780
Nozomi, is that okay?

00:08:08.780 --> 00:08:11.324
Huh? Yeah, sure.

00:08:16.954 --> 00:08:18.081
Something's off.

00:08:18.081 --> 00:08:19.332
Off?

00:08:19.332 --> 00:08:20.625
You mean Eli-chan?

00:08:20.625 --> 00:08:25.505
Isn't it weird for Eli to take the
initiative and insist on a love song?

00:08:25.505 --> 00:08:28.716
She must really want to make it to Love Live.

00:08:28.716 --> 00:08:30.802
Then we should stop her.

00:08:30.802 --> 00:08:32.095
No matter how you look at it,

00:08:32.095 --> 00:08:35.139
we'd put on a much more polished
performance with an existing song.

00:08:35.139 --> 00:08:37.600
You mean what she said
about trusting Nozomi-chan?

00:08:37.600 --> 00:08:41.104
Have you seen her be that particular before?

00:08:41.104 --> 00:08:42.897
Then why?

00:08:42.897 --> 00:08:44.857
I don't know.

00:08:44.857 --> 00:08:46.234
Maybe...

00:08:47.527 --> 00:08:50.822
Sorry for deceiving you.

00:08:50.822 --> 00:08:52.365
Khorosho...

00:08:52.907 --> 00:08:57.161
If Eli joins them, there's no way we can win!

00:08:57.161 --> 00:09:00.289
What are you imagining?
That would never happen.

00:09:00.289 --> 00:09:01.249
Then...

00:09:01.749 --> 00:09:05.586
I don't know, but there must be some reason.

00:09:08.131 --> 00:09:09.090
Eli-chi.

00:09:10.716 --> 00:09:11.592
What's wrong?

00:09:12.051 --> 00:09:14.762
Aren't you being too pushy?

00:09:14.762 --> 00:09:17.348
Everyone seems to be at a loss.

00:09:17.348 --> 00:09:19.851
It's fine. This is what I want to do.

00:09:21.102 --> 00:09:23.229
Haven't you always wanted to do it?

00:09:23.896 --> 00:09:25.022
See you later.

00:09:29.443 --> 00:09:33.823
For crying out loud...
You're such a busybody, Eli-chi...

00:09:37.326 --> 00:09:38.744
Love Live!

00:09:45.376 --> 00:09:47.420
I like you! I love you!

00:09:50.256 --> 00:09:55.428
- This isn't right!
- W-Well, you're not wrong...

00:09:57.013 --> 00:09:59.432
Love songs are hard.

00:09:59.807 --> 00:10:04.770
Most love songs are about the
way you express your love.

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:07.481
They might be difficult for a
straightforward person like you.

00:10:07.481 --> 00:10:10.484
She's not straightforward, she's just simple.

00:10:10.484 --> 00:10:13.279
You say that, but your notebook is blank, too.

00:10:13.279 --> 00:10:14.530
I-I'm about to start writing!

00:10:15.031 --> 00:10:19.994
Now, now. Why don't we watch a
romantic movie to inspire ourselves?

00:10:19.994 --> 00:10:22.121
A romantic movie, huh?

00:10:24.457 --> 00:10:25.875
Poor thing...

00:10:37.887 --> 00:10:40.681
What the heck? What a cheap story!

00:10:40.681 --> 00:10:42.516
You're crying.

00:10:48.439 --> 00:10:52.235
Why are you hiding? It's not a scary movie.

00:10:52.235 --> 00:10:55.071
Yeah. It's an emotional scene.

00:10:55.071 --> 00:10:57.990
I know! I-It's embarrassing...

00:11:16.384 --> 00:11:17.134
Umi-chan!?

00:11:17.134 --> 00:11:19.470
It's too embarrassing! It's shameless!

00:11:19.470 --> 00:11:21.305
You think so?

00:11:21.305 --> 00:11:22.390
Yes!

00:11:22.390 --> 00:11:25.559
This isn't something you should do in public!

00:11:25.977 --> 00:11:26.894
Huh?

00:11:28.354 --> 00:11:29.855
Is it over?

00:11:29.855 --> 00:11:33.067
Honoka-chan, you fell asleep
three minutes into the movie.

00:11:33.067 --> 00:11:38.197
Sorry. I thought, "What a slow movie,"
and started feeling sleepy...

00:11:38.197 --> 00:11:41.701
Real life isn't like the movies.

00:11:41.701 --> 00:11:44.287
Let's try coming up with lyrics again, and—

00:11:44.287 --> 00:11:45.121
Wait.

00:11:46.998 --> 00:11:49.041
Maybe we should give up.

00:11:49.500 --> 00:11:51.585
We can't compose a new song

00:11:51.585 --> 00:11:54.088
and then start practicing the
choreography and singing now.

00:11:54.088 --> 00:11:56.382
It'll look unpolished.

00:11:57.341 --> 00:11:58.092
But—

00:11:58.092 --> 00:12:00.052
Actually, I agree.

00:12:00.845 --> 00:12:05.558
We don't have to rely on a love song.
We have our own music.

00:12:06.392 --> 00:12:08.019
Yeah.

00:12:08.019 --> 00:12:09.603
We're up against A-RISE.

00:12:09.603 --> 00:12:11.856
Cheap tricks won't work against them.

00:12:11.856 --> 00:12:12.773
But—

00:12:12.773 --> 00:12:15.526
Everyone's right.

00:12:15.526 --> 00:12:18.446
We should put all of our
efforts into an existing song.

00:12:19.780 --> 00:12:20.781
Nozomi...

00:12:20.781 --> 00:12:23.534
That's what the cards are telling me to do.

00:12:23.534 --> 00:12:25.411
Wait, Nozomi. You—

00:12:25.411 --> 00:12:29.874
It's fine. What's more important than u's?

00:12:33.210 --> 00:12:34.587
Is something wrong?

00:12:34.587 --> 00:12:36.756
No, it's nothing.

00:12:36.756 --> 00:12:41.052
Let's call it a day and
start practicing tomorrow.

00:12:42.470 --> 00:12:43.888
See you later!

00:12:43.888 --> 00:12:45.514
Bye-bye!

00:12:48.642 --> 00:12:52.271
Rin, Hanayo, you go on ahead.

00:13:01.489 --> 00:13:02.907
Are you sure?

00:13:02.907 --> 00:13:04.533
I said it's fine.

00:13:04.533 --> 00:13:05.451
You should say something.

00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:09.080
If you do, I'm sure they'll support you.

00:13:09.747 --> 00:13:12.208
This is all I need.

00:13:13.334 --> 00:13:14.293
You're so stubborn...

00:13:14.752 --> 00:13:16.670
You're one to talk.

00:13:18.255 --> 00:13:19.423
What does that mean?

00:13:21.759 --> 00:13:23.219
See you tomorrow.

00:13:23.219 --> 00:13:24.553
Nozomi...

00:13:25.388 --> 00:13:26.597
Wait.

00:13:28.182 --> 00:13:29.100
Maki-chan...

00:13:29.642 --> 00:13:34.021
You told me before that I'm troublesome.

00:13:34.021 --> 00:13:35.356
Did 17

00:13:36.899 --> 00:13:39.110
You're way more troublesome than I am.

00:13:41.153 --> 00:13:42.696
I feel the same way.

00:13:42.696 --> 00:13:43.948
And I agree.

00:13:48.536 --> 00:13:50.121
Pardon the intrusion.

00:13:50.121 --> 00:13:51.705
Make yourselves at home.

00:13:54.250 --> 00:13:55.459
Is tea okay?

00:13:56.544 --> 00:13:57.044
Yeah.

00:13:58.337 --> 00:14:01.006
Do you live alone?

00:14:01.590 --> 00:14:02.299
Yes.

00:14:05.678 --> 00:14:10.808
Ever since I was little, I transferred schools
a lot because of my parents' work.

00:14:11.809 --> 00:14:12.643
I see...

00:14:12.643 --> 00:14:17.064
She finally found a place she belonged
when she came to Otonokizaka High.

00:14:17.064 --> 00:14:19.358
Don't talk about that.

00:14:19.358 --> 00:14:22.236
It's not something we should discuss now.

00:14:22.236 --> 00:14:23.404
Whoops.

00:14:24.864 --> 00:14:26.115
Tell me.

00:14:26.657 --> 00:14:28.909
We've come this far.

00:14:28.909 --> 00:14:32.288
She's right. There's no
point in hiding it, is there?

00:14:32.872 --> 00:14:36.459
I wasn't hiding it...

00:14:36.917 --> 00:14:39.462
You just made a big deal out of it.

00:14:40.087 --> 00:14:41.255
Liar.

00:14:41.255 --> 00:14:45.050
Haven't you been looking
forward to it since p's formed?

00:14:45.926 --> 00:14:47.553
That's not true.

00:14:47.553 --> 00:14:48.471
Nozomi!

00:14:49.513 --> 00:14:52.975
I just had a little wish.

00:14:52.975 --> 00:14:54.602
That's enough!

00:14:54.602 --> 00:14:57.229
I don't know where you're going with this!

00:14:57.229 --> 00:14:57.980
What do you mean!?

00:14:59.857 --> 00:15:00.941
Nozomi!

00:15:03.152 --> 00:15:07.323
Simply put, it was Nozomi's dream.

00:15:07.323 --> 00:15:07.865
Eli-chi.

00:15:08.365 --> 00:15:11.827
We can't not tell her anything now.

00:15:12.453 --> 00:15:14.580
Her dream? To sing a love song?

00:15:15.289 --> 00:15:20.044
No. The love song part doesn't matter.

00:15:22.129 --> 00:15:24.840
It's writing a song as nine.

00:15:27.468 --> 00:15:31.805
Weaving together each
member's words and feelings.

00:15:33.015 --> 00:15:35.768
A song we truly wrote together.

00:15:36.435 --> 00:15:38.145
She wanted to write a song like that.

00:15:38.145 --> 00:15:40.397
She wanted to go to Love Live with that song.

00:15:41.232 --> 00:15:43.234
That was Nozomi's dream.

00:15:43.943 --> 00:15:47.196
That's why I suggested a love song.

00:15:47.196 --> 00:15:49.031
It didn't go over well, though.

00:15:50.074 --> 00:15:54.578
If we could just compose a single
song from everyone's ideas...

00:15:56.413 --> 00:15:57.456
I told you.

00:15:57.957 --> 00:16:02.503
I never said it was anything
as big as a dream.

00:16:02.503 --> 00:16:03.796
Then what is it?

00:16:06.924 --> 00:16:08.050
I don't know...

00:16:08.926 --> 00:16:11.512
But it doesn't have to be a song.

00:16:11.512 --> 00:16:18.060
It would have been enough for the nine
of us to make something together.

00:16:18.727 --> 00:16:21.981
To me, these nine members are a miracle...

00:16:21.981 --> 00:16:23.148
A miracle?

00:16:23.983 --> 00:16:29.738
Yes. U's is my miracle...

00:16:30.573 --> 00:16:33.617
Let me introduce you to your new friend

00:16:33.617 --> 00:16:35.536
Nozomi Tojo
who transferred here today.

00:16:36.036 --> 00:16:37.830
Be nice to her.

00:16:39.832 --> 00:16:42.751
Because I was always transferring,
I didn't have friends.

00:16:58.934 --> 00:17:01.478
Naturally, no one understood me.

00:17:10.988 --> 00:17:12.948
Hello, everyone.

00:17:13.365 --> 00:17:16.201
My name is Ayase Eli.
Nice to meet you.

00:17:18.078 --> 00:17:19.455
I met her for the first time.

00:17:20.080 --> 00:17:24.084
To protect herself, she
distanced herself from others.

00:17:24.084 --> 00:17:25.961
She didn't fit in with others.

00:17:27.004 --> 00:17:28.464
She's straightforward.

00:17:28.881 --> 00:17:31.884
She was just like me.

00:17:33.093 --> 00:17:35.512
She had stronger opinions
than others around her.

00:17:35.512 --> 00:17:38.432
Her awkwardness made
her clash with people.

00:17:39.767 --> 00:17:40.684
Excuse me!

00:17:44.396 --> 00:17:45.314
Who are you?

00:17:46.231 --> 00:17:48.025
I I...

00:17:52.321 --> 00:17:54.323
I'm Tojo Nozomi.

00:17:55.574 --> 00:17:58.327
That was how Eli-chi and I met.

00:18:00.162 --> 00:18:06.210
Later, I met others who felt the same way,
but I couldn't reach out to them.

00:18:07.336 --> 00:18:13.926
When I saw you, there was passion,
but I didn't know how to reach out to you.

00:18:13.926 --> 00:18:15.260
Recruiting members!

00:18:15.678 --> 00:18:19.348
There were girls like that here and there.

00:18:22.059 --> 00:18:28.315
That's when a presence arrived to tie
us all together with great strength.

00:18:28.315 --> 00:18:32.736
A presence that connects these people
who all share the same feelings.

00:18:33.612 --> 00:18:35.739
I was determined to make it happen.

00:18:36.198 --> 00:18:39.368
I wanted to accomplish
something together as nine.

00:18:42.579 --> 00:18:47.084
It might've been nice if it was a song.

00:18:48.085 --> 00:18:54.883
But even if it's not, y's has already
created something enormous.

00:18:56.510 --> 00:19:00.931
That's enough for me.
My dream has already—!

00:19:24.121 --> 00:19:26.749
My greatest dream has already...

00:19:28.417 --> 00:19:30.711
So that's the end of that.

00:19:31.336 --> 00:19:32.880
Are you satisfied?

00:19:33.922 --> 00:19:36.592
So says Nozomi.

00:19:36.592 --> 00:19:37.384
What do you think?

00:19:43.265 --> 00:19:45.976
Are you going to call everyone here?

00:19:46.435 --> 00:19:49.688
Why not invite everyone at least once?

00:19:50.773 --> 00:19:52.941
They're your friends.

00:19:55.986 --> 00:19:57.321
What!?

00:19:57.321 --> 00:19:59.531
We're writing one after all?

00:19:59.531 --> 00:20:01.825
Yeah. We're all going to write it together.

00:20:02.534 --> 00:20:05.579
Nozomi-chan lives by herself...

00:20:05.579 --> 00:20:07.080
I had no idea.

00:20:07.080 --> 00:20:09.041
Did something happen, Maki-chan?

00:20:09.041 --> 00:20:11.210
No, nothing.

00:20:11.210 --> 00:20:13.545
It's just a little Christmas present.

00:20:13.545 --> 00:20:17.299
From p's to the goddess who created y's.

00:20:20.719 --> 00:20:23.555
We're all contributing lyrics, huh?

00:20:27.184 --> 00:20:28.435
Is this...?

00:20:32.898 --> 00:20:33.857
Nozomi-chan!

00:20:35.192 --> 00:20:37.653
I'm surprised you have that out.

00:20:37.653 --> 00:20:42.157
S-So, what? Even I do that...

00:20:43.450 --> 00:20:45.786
After all, you are my friends.

00:20:46.411 --> 00:20:47.746
Nozomi-chan!

00:20:48.831 --> 00:20:51.041
So cute!

00:20:51.041 --> 00:20:53.293
Don't laugh!

00:20:53.293 --> 00:20:54.962
You're speaking differently!

00:20:57.840 --> 00:20:59.424
Don't struggle.

00:21:00.008 --> 00:21:02.344
You need this kind of thing once in a while.

00:21:06.181 --> 00:21:07.432
Sheesh...

00:21:10.185 --> 00:21:11.812
Look!

00:21:39.172 --> 00:21:40.007
Desire.

00:21:45.345 --> 00:21:46.555
Melody.

00:21:48.390 --> 00:21:49.558
Premonition.

00:21:51.351 --> 00:21:52.561
Mystery.

00:21:54.104 --> 00:21:55.314
Future.

00:21:56.815 --> 00:21:58.066
Thrill.

00:21:59.443 --> 00:22:00.569
Sky.

00:22:01.862 --> 00:22:03.071
Feelings.

00:22:09.369 --> 00:22:10.579
Love.

00:22:15.125 --> 00:22:20.923
Ureshiikara kimi ni ai ni ikou
Because I'm happy, I'll go see you

00:22:20.923 --> 00:22:26.678
sabishiikara kimi ni ai ni ikou (ai ni ikuyo)
Because I'm lonely, I'll go see you (I'll go see you)

00:22:27.095 --> 00:22:29.932
Sonna kimochi ni narunda
That's how I feel

00:22:29.932 --> 00:22:32.935
susumu toki nayamu toki Whether I'm
making progress or hung up on something,

00:22:32.935 --> 00:22:36.939
tsunagatteirundane zutto
We're always connected

00:22:38.482 --> 00:22:44.071
<i>honki no yume de (HI LETS GO) asu wo tsukamu (HI GO GO) With
a true dream, (Hi! Let's go') seize tomorrow (Hi' Go, go')</i>

00:22:44.071 --> 00:22:51.536
Kitto dekiruyo kimi nara
I'm sure you can do it

00:22:53.997 --> 00:22:59.795
tama ni wa yukkuri kimi no pehsu de
Sometimes, take your time at your own pace

00:22:59.795 --> 00:23:05.592
yaritai kototachi mitsumetegoran
To look at all the things you want to do

00:23:05.592 --> 00:23:12.641
sono ato ganbare zenryokudene (ganbarouyo) Then do
your best! With all your strength (Let's do our best)

00:23:12.641 --> 00:23:21.733
Kibun ga harete ohzora e maiagaruyo Once you've
cleared your head, you'll fly up into the sky

00:23:22.275 --> 00:23:32.661
donna toki datte kimi wo mitsumeteru
I'm always looking at you

00:23:35.998 --> 00:23:39.459
Next time on Love Live!
"Melody of the Heart"
